Title:
Hunt-Weird-Syscalls

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
This repository is an ETW-based proof-of-concept that detects “abnormal” Windows syscalls associated with direct and indirect syscall techniques commonly used to evade user-mode hooks. It leverages kernel ETW providers so emitted events include call stacks that reveal the user-mode return address/module responsible for the syscall. The POC currently monitors `NtOpenThread` and `NtSetContextThread` via the `Microsoft-Windows-Kernel-Audit-API-Calls` provider, flagging (1) syscalls originating from untrusted modules (direct syscalls) and (2) mismatches between the expected ntdll stub and the syscall actually executed (indirect syscalls). It enables stack traces using `EVENT_ENABLE_PROPERTY_STACK_TRACE` to support attribution. The repo includes test binaries generated with SysWhispers3 to demonstrate detection of both syscall styles. It’s primarily useful for Blue Teams/EDR engineers and defenders building telemetry for syscall-evasion tradecraft, but also informative for red teamers validating detectability.

Technical Focus:
- Kernel ETW telemetry for API/syscall auditing
- Detecting direct syscalls via untrusted callsite/module attribution
- Detecting indirect syscalls via ntdll stub vs executed syscall mismatch
- `Microsoft-Windows-Kernel-Audit-API-Calls` provider usage
- Stack-walk/call trace collection (`EVENT_ENABLE_PROPERTY_STACK_TRACE`)
- SysWhispers3-generated syscall stubs (jumper/embedded)

Use Cases:
- Build/validate detections for direct/indirect syscall evasion techniques
- Hunt for suspicious thread operations (`OpenThread`, `SetContextThread`) indicative of injection/manipulation
- Prototype ETW-based enrichment for EDR sensors (callsite/module attribution)
- Regression testing of syscall-evasion PoCs against defensive telemetry

Keywords:
ETW, Event Tracing for Windows, Microsoft-Windows-Kernel-Audit-API-Calls, kernel provider, stack trace, call stack, EVENT_ENABLE_PROPERTY_STACK_TRACE, syscalls, direct syscall, indirect syscall, NtOpenThread, NtSetContextThread, OpenThread, SetContextThread, ntdll, syscall stub, SysWhispers3, KrabsETW, Windows 10 19044, IOC hunting